{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>וישבו.</b> To their rear — toward the Egyptian side they would advance each third day, in order to mislead Pharaoh so that he would say, 'They are astray in the land,' as it is said: ״וְאָמַר פַּרְעֹה לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ and so forth." "<b>ויחנו לפני פי החירת.</b> It is Pithom, and now it is called Pi HaChirot because the Israelites were made free there. And they are two towering crags standing upright, and the valley between them is called Pi HaSela'im." "<b>לפני בעל צפן.</b> It alone survived of all the gods of Egypt, in order to mislead them, so that they would say, 'Their fear is mighty.' And concerning it Job explained: ״מַשְׂגִּיא לַגּוֹיִם וַיְאַבְּדֵם״ (Job 12)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:04.069317439Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}